-- title:
--   Nonzero simultaneous Hecke eigenspace in K⊗ Tₚ J
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $J$ be an additive commutative group carrying a module structure over [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16), the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell,Y_d]$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ in indeterminates indexed by $\mathrm{Primes}\sqcup\mathbb{N}$ (the free Hecke–diamond algebra). Write $T=$ [`TateModule p J`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) for the group of sequences $(x_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ in $J$ with $p^n x_n=0$ and $p\,x_{n+1}=x_n$, regarded as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and assume $T$ is finite and free over $\mathbb{Z}_p$. Each $t$ acts on $T$ by $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear endomorphisms via `tateHeckeRepOne`, namely termwise by the action of $t$ on $J$; `rationalHeckeRepOne` is the induced action on $\mathbb{Q}_p\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T$, and `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne` is the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra $A$ of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T)$ generated by its image. Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra, and let $\Lambda\colon A\to K$ be a ring homomorphism such that $\Lambda$ of the image of $c\in\mathbb{Z}_p$ under $\mathbb{Q}_p\to A$ equals the image of $c$ under $\mathbb{Z}_p\to K$. Then the infimum over all $t$ of the kernels of $\widehat{t}-\Lambda(t)\cdot\mathrm{id}$ on $K\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T$, where $\widehat{t}$ is the base change to $K$ of the action of $t$ on $T$, is not the zero submodule.
--
--   This is the existence of a nonzero simultaneous eigenvector in $K\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}T_pJ$ for a commuting family of Hecke–diamond operators with prescribed eigenvalue character $\Lambda$. It is the first half of the statement [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.iInf_ker_hecke_sub_ne_bot_and_inf_span_eq_bot_tateModule_jOne`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.iInf_ker_hecke_sub_ne_bot_and_inf_span_eq_bot_tateModule_jOne), used in cutting out the Galois representation attached to a primitive form from the Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_1(M)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_iInf_ker_tateHeckeRepOne_baseChange_sub_ne_bot.lean

